{"key": "5bfae215e2b674f3", "role": "operator", "t": 1790981143.715, "seconds": 10.465, "output": "```python\nimport json\n\ndef check_similarity(PURPOSE, Entity):\n    # Check if inputs are strings\n    if isinstance(PURPOSE, str) and isinstance(Entity, str):\n        # If both are strings, check if they are equal\n        if PURPOSE == Entity:\n            return 1\n        else:\n            return 0\n    \n    # Check if inputs are JSON tuples (lists in Python)\n    elif isinstance(PURPOSE, list) and isinstance(Entity, list):\n        # If both are lists, check if they have the same elements\n        if set(PURPOSE) == set(Entity):\n            return 1\n        else:\n            return 0\n    \n    # If inputs are neither strings nor lists, return 0\n    else:\n        return 0\n\n# Test the function\nPURPOSE = \"test\"\nEntity = \"test\"\nprint(check_similarity(PURPOSE, Entity))\n\nPURPOSE = [\"test\", \"example\"]\nEntity = [\"example\", \"test\"]\nprint(check_similarity(PURPOSE, Entity))\n\nPURPOSE = \"test\"\nEntity = [\"example\", \"test\"]\nprint(check_similarity(PURPOSE, Entity))\n```"}
